## Layout

```
{{ experiment_name }}/
  register.py        # registers this recipe with the core
  hpo/               # Optuna sweep (DEFAULT workflow): study/objective/search_space
  episodes.py        # build_episodes — {{ anchoring_strategy }} anchoring
  eval.py            # evaluate — model -> metrics
  summarize.py       # {{ summarizer_class }} — runs -> leaderboard CSV
  configs/           # data/ models/ sweeps/ (experiment-owned)
  results/           # run output (gitignored; README only)
  trained_models/    # checkpoints (gitignored; README only)
  scripts/ docs/     # experiment-specific tooling and notes
```

## Getting started

The **Optuna sweep is the default workflow**. To stand it up:

1. Implement the sweep stubs in `hpo/`: `build_data` + the search space
   (`study.py` / `search_space.py`) and the per-trial `objective.py` (build/train
   a model from the suggested config and return its `{{ primary_metric }}`).
2. Implement the recipe stubs: `build_episodes` (`episodes.py`), `evaluate`
   (`eval.py`), and `_parse_run_dir` (`summarize.py`).
3. Add data/model configs under `configs/`.
4. Run the sweep:
   `scripts/sweeps/optuna/launch_sweep.sh` (or
   `python -m experiments.{{ experiment_name }}.hpo.study run --n-trials 50`).
   Run outputs resolve under this experiment's `results/` and `trained_models/`.

